# Night moments (moments.ron, design/handson.md §5, §11.1): .title (marker hover), .text (the card),
# .opt.<option> (button), .result.<option> (the line after), .expired (when nobody came in time).
# English placeholder texts in every language until T9 (see handson_TODO.txt).

# --- m_record_request ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
moment.m_record_request.title
* A record request

moment.m_record_request.text
* "Karolina, have you got something a bit… you know. Like the old days?"

moment.m_record_request.opt.put_on
* Put it on

moment.m_record_request.opt.later
* Maybe later

moment.m_record_request.result.put_on
* The needle drops. Someone at the window table starts tapping along.

moment.m_record_request.result.later
* "Later, then. I'm not going anywhere."

# --- m_blackout_candles -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
moment.m_blackout_candles.title
* The lights went out

moment.m_blackout_candles.text
* The hall goes dark. Grandma's candles are in the drawer under the till, where they always were.

moment.m_blackout_candles.opt.candles
* Light the candles

moment.m_blackout_candles.opt.torch
* The old torch will do

moment.m_blackout_candles.result.candles
* Table by table, the café comes back — smaller, warmer, gold.

moment.m_blackout_candles.result.torch
* One beam of light and a lot of patient faces.

moment.m_blackout_candles.expired
* Someone found the candles and lit them for you.

# --- m_leak_bucket ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
moment.m_leak_bucket.title
* The roof is leaking

moment.m_leak_bucket.text
* Plink. Plink. A drop lands right where people walk.

moment.m_leak_bucket.opt.bucket
* Put a bucket under it

moment.m_leak_bucket.opt.roofer
* Call a roofer

moment.m_leak_bucket.result.bucket
* The plinks turn into a little tune.

moment.m_leak_bucket.result.roofer
* A roofer climbs up in the rain. The plinking stops for good.

moment.m_leak_bucket.expired
* Someone put a bucket under it.

# --- m_station_cat -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
moment.m_station_cat.title
* Someone with whiskers

moment.m_station_cat.text
* The station cat sits by the door, wet and dignified, pretending not to look at you.

moment.m_station_cat.opt.milk
* A saucer of milk

moment.m_station_cat.opt.ham
* A bit of ham

moment.m_station_cat.opt.scratch
* Scratch its ears

moment.m_station_cat.result.milk
* Lap, lap, lap. A slow blink — that's a thank-you in cat.

moment.m_station_cat.result.ham
* The ham is gone before it lands. The cat stays a little longer.

moment.m_station_cat.result.scratch
* If it knows you, it leans in. If it doesn't, it leaves with great dignity.

moment.m_station_cat.expired
* Someone left a saucer by the door.

# --- m_lost_traveller ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
moment.m_lost_traveller.title
* A lost traveller

moment.m_lost_traveller.text
* A traveller stands in the doorway with a suitcase and a crumpled ticket, looking for the right platform.

moment.m_lost_traveller.opt.app
* Check the Shiftella app

moment.m_lost_traveller.opt.napkin_map
* Draw a map on a napkin

moment.m_lost_traveller.result.app
* The right train, the right platform, three minutes to spare. They leave a tip and a grin.

moment.m_lost_traveller.result.napkin_map
* A napkin map with a little star on the platform. They keep it.

# --- m_stuffy_window -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
moment.m_stuffy_window.title
* It's stuffy in here

moment.m_stuffy_window.text
* So many people, so much steam. The windows are crying.

moment.m_stuffy_window.opt.open
* Open the window

moment.m_stuffy_window.opt.leave
* Leave it

moment.m_stuffy_window.result.open
* Cool air and the smell of rain. Someone orders something cold.

moment.m_stuffy_window.result.leave
* Cosy, if a little sticky.

# --- m_fogged_window -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
moment.m_fogged_window.title
* The glass has fogged up

moment.m_fogged_window.text
* A train is coming. You can hear it, but you can't see it through the fogged glass.

moment.m_fogged_window.opt.wipe
* Wipe the glass

moment.m_fogged_window.result.wipe
* Just in time — the train's light sweeps through the whole room.

# --- m_sleeping_guest -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
moment.m_sleeping_guest.title
* Someone fell asleep

moment.m_sleeping_guest.text
* A guest has dozed off over an empty cup, head on their arm.

moment.m_sleeping_guest.opt.blanket
* Cover them with a blanket

moment.m_sleeping_guest.opt.let_sleep
* Let them sleep

moment.m_sleeping_guest.opt.water
* A glass of water, gently

moment.m_sleeping_guest.result.blanket
* Grandma's checked blanket. They don't wake, but they smile.

moment.m_sleeping_guest.result.let_sleep
* The rain does the rest.

moment.m_sleeping_guest.result.water
* They wake slowly, drink, and leave lighter than they came.

# --- m_drone_wrong_address ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
moment.m_drone_wrong_address.title
* A lost delivery drone

moment.m_drone_wrong_address.text
* A delivery drone taps the window, blinking "address not found". It has a small parcel.

moment.m_drone_wrong_address.opt.reroute
* Re-route it in the Shiftella app

moment.m_drone_wrong_address.opt.keep
* Keep the parcel for pickup

moment.m_drone_wrong_address.result.reroute
* It beeps twice — a thank-you, probably — and hums off over the roofs.

moment.m_drone_wrong_address.result.keep
* The parcel waits behind the counter. Someone will come for it.

moment.m_drone_wrong_address.expired
* The drone found its own way. Somebody waved it off.

moment.m_drone_wrong_address.thanks
* A message from the drone's owner: "Thanks for the re-route!" and 50 Kč.

moment.m_drone_wrong_address.parcel
* The parcel's owner came by and left a jar of butterfly pea flowers. "For the trouble."

moment.m_drone_wrong_address.collected
* The parcel's owner came by, thanked you and left a tip.

# --- m_coffee_for_helper ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
moment.m_coffee_for_helper.title
* A tired helper

moment.m_coffee_for_helper.text
* Your helper is moving slower, rubbing their eyes when they think nobody sees.

moment.m_coffee_for_helper.opt.coffee
* Make them a coffee

moment.m_coffee_for_helper.opt.break
* Send them on a break

moment.m_coffee_for_helper.result.coffee
* "For me? You didn't have to." They hold the cup with both hands.

moment.m_coffee_for_helper.result.break
* Ten minutes on the back step. They come back humming.

# --- m_hang_garlands -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
moment.m_hang_garlands.title
* A box marked "Vánoce — L."

moment.m_hang_garlands.text
* Grandma's Christmas box is on the counter: garlands, tiny lights and a note — "windows first".

moment.m_hang_garlands.opt.hang
* Hang them up

moment.m_hang_garlands.result.hang
* Windows, counter, door. The café looks like it remembered something.

moment.m_hang_garlands.expired
* The crew will hang them in the morning.

# --- m_leak_empty ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
moment.m_leak_empty.title
* The bucket is full

moment.m_leak_empty.text
* The bucket under the leak is nearly overflowing.

moment.m_leak_empty.opt.empty
* Empty it

moment.m_leak_empty.result.empty
* Emptied, back in place. The tune starts over.

# --- m_busker -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
moment.m_busker.title
* A busker in the rain

moment.m_busker.text
* Someone is playing under the station awning, a guitar case open, rain on the strings.

moment.m_busker.opt.tea
* Bring them a tea

moment.m_busker.opt.coin
* A coin in the case

moment.m_busker.opt.ask_in
* Ask them in to play

moment.m_busker.result.tea
* They nod a thank-you and play one more song, just for the window.

moment.m_busker.result.coin
* The coin clinks. The song goes on.

moment.m_busker.result.ask_in
* They shake off the rain and play by the stage. The hall comes alive.

# --- m_first_snow ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
moment.m_first_snow.title
* It's snowing

moment.m_first_snow.text
* The first snow of the year is falling past grandma's window, slow and silent.

moment.m_first_snow.opt.call_all
* Call everyone to look

moment.m_first_snow.opt.candle
* A candle in the window

moment.m_first_snow.result.call_all
* Guests, crew, even the cat — everyone at the window, saying nothing at all.

moment.m_first_snow.result.candle
* A small flame against the snow. People outside slow down to look.

moment.m_first_snow.expired
* The snow kept falling. Nobody minded.

# --- m_umbrellas ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
moment.m_umbrellas.title
* Wet umbrellas everywhere

moment.m_umbrellas.text
* A downpour, and every guest brings half of it in with them.

moment.m_umbrellas.opt.stand
* Put out the umbrella stand

moment.m_umbrellas.opt.newspapers
* Newspapers on the floor

moment.m_umbrellas.result.stand
* Umbrellas in a row, dripping politely.

moment.m_umbrellas.result.newspapers
* Yesterday's news, today's doormat. Vera approves.

# --- m_forgotten_item ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
moment.m_forgotten_item.title
* Something left behind

moment.m_forgotten_item.text
* An umbrella hangs from an empty chair. Its owner is just crossing the street.

moment.m_forgotten_item.opt.run
* Run after them

moment.m_forgotten_item.opt.lost_found
* The lost & found box

moment.m_forgotten_item.result.run
* You catch them at the crossing. They laugh, and press a coin into your hand.

moment.m_forgotten_item.result.lost_found
* Into the box. They came back for it before dawn.

moment.m_forgotten_item.expired
* It went into the lost & found box. Its owner came back for it.

# --- m_dead_phone -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
moment.m_dead_phone.title
* A dead phone

moment.m_dead_phone.text
* A guest stares at a black screen. Their ticket, their map, their whole night is on it.

moment.m_dead_phone.opt.charger
* Lend the counter charger

moment.m_dead_phone.opt.socket
* Point to the socket table

moment.m_dead_phone.result.charger
* Two per cent, five per cent, saved.

moment.m_dead_phone.result.socket
* They move tables, relieved.

# --- m_tired_parent ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
moment.m_tired_parent.title
* A tired parent

moment.m_tired_parent.text
* A parent off the train, a sleepy child on their lap, both too tired to order.

moment.m_tired_parent.opt.warm_milk
* Warm milk, on the house

moment.m_tired_parent.opt.blanket
* A blanket for the little one

moment.m_tired_parent.result.warm_milk
* The little one drinks half and falls asleep. The parent mouths "thank you".

moment.m_tired_parent.result.blanket
* Tucked in like a small parcel. The parent finally sits back.

# --- m_delay_board ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
moment.m_delay_board.title
* The trains are late

moment.m_delay_board.text
* The station board blinks DELAYED. A café full of people who meant to be somewhere else.

moment.m_delay_board.opt.refills
* Free refills for the waiting

moment.m_delay_board.opt.board
* Put the station board on the café screen

moment.m_delay_board.result.refills
* Nobody minds waiting quite so much.

moment.m_delay_board.result.board
* Now everyone can see the minutes tick down. Fewer anxious glances at the door.

# --- m_radio_tuning ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
moment.m_radio_tuning.title
* Grandma's radio

moment.m_radio_tuning.text
* The old radio crackles between stations. The dial is warm under your fingers.

moment.m_radio_tuning.opt.jazz
* Night jazz

moment.m_radio_tuning.opt.waltz
* An old waltz

moment.m_radio_tuning.opt.static
* Static…

moment.m_radio_tuning.result.jazz
* A piano, somewhere far away, playing just for the night shift.

moment.m_radio_tuning.result.waltz
* Grandma's waltz, thin and silver through the old speaker.

moment.m_radio_tuning.result.static
* Rain through the speaker, and for a second a voice: "…osobní vlak Rn 333, nástupiště dvě…" Then nothing.

# --- m_bulb_flicker -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
moment.m_bulb_flicker.title
* The window lamp flickers

moment.m_bulb_flicker.text
* The light in the window stutters once, twice.

moment.m_bulb_flicker.opt.spare_bulb
* Grandma's spare bulb

moment.m_bulb_flicker.result.spare_bulb
* There's a box of spares in the drawer, labelled in her hand. She kept spares for sixty years.

# --- m_parcel_lviv ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
moment.m_parcel_lviv.title
* A parcel from Lviv

moment.m_parcel_lviv.text
* A parcel for Oleh, tied with string, smelling of dried pears. His mother's handwriting on top.

moment.m_parcel_lviv.opt.open
* Open it with Oleh

moment.m_parcel_lviv.opt.morning
* Save it for the morning

moment.m_parcel_lviv.result.open
* Dried fruit, beetroot, a jar of honey and a note he reads twice. "She says to feed you too."

moment.m_parcel_lviv.result.morning
* It waits on the shelf until the morning. Oleh keeps glancing at it.

moment.m_parcel_lviv.expired
* Oleh opened it in the morning and shared everything.

# --- m_advent_candle --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
moment.m_advent_candle.title
* The Advent wreath

moment.m_advent_candle.text
* Grandma's wreath on the counter, the next candle waiting.

moment.m_advent_candle.opt.light
* Light the candle

moment.m_advent_candle.result.light
* One more small flame. The counter glows a little warmer.

# --- m_mikulas -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
moment.m_mikulas.title
* Mikuláš, an angel and a devil

moment.m_mikulas.text
* Three students in costume burst in from the snow: "A poem for something warm?"

moment.m_mikulas.opt.cocoa
* Hot chocolate on the house

moment.m_mikulas.opt.kolac
* A koláč for each

moment.m_mikulas.opt.applause
* Just applause

moment.m_mikulas.result.cocoa
* The devil recites the poem, the angel forgets the words, Mikuláš drinks the most.

moment.m_mikulas.result.kolac
* Three koláče, three bows, one very sticky devil.

moment.m_mikulas.result.applause
* The whole café claps. The devil takes a bow.

# --- m_cat_name -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
moment.m_cat_name.title
* The cat needs a name

moment.m_cat_name.text
* The cat lives here now. Everyone agrees. It's time it had a name.

moment.m_cat_name.opt.vlak
* Vlak

moment.m_cat_name.opt.kofi
* Kofi

moment.m_cat_name.opt.lidka
* Lidka

moment.m_cat_name.result.vlak
* Vlak, like the trains it watches. It doesn't look up. That means yes.

moment.m_cat_name.result.kofi
* Kofi. It sniffs your cup as if to confirm.

moment.m_cat_name.result.lidka
* Lidka. It curls up in grandma's chair, as if it always knew.
